  "name": "Easily Understand How to Play Pokémon Cards Magazine",
  "category": "publication_promotion",
  "description": {
    "text": "Easily Understand How to Play Pokémon Cards is a guide to the card game from Media Factory, the game's Japanese publisher. Its first edition, of 30 November 1996, came with non-glossy prints of the first two promos, Ivy Pikachu and Jigglypuff, which CoroCoro Comic had given glossy the month before; it is the only non-glossy Ivy Pikachu, and it corrects the artist credit to Keiji Kinebuchi. The Latest Edition, released on 13 November 1998, came with Diglett and Dugtrio, in art never printed in English and used again on the e-Card layout in the Japanese Pokémon Web expansion.",
